  "narrative": {
    "intro": "National Steel and Shipbuilding obligated $2.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. National Steel and Shipbuilding won 16 awards this period, with an average award size of $174M, and obligations are up 406.3% year over year. National Steel and Shipbuilding’s recent federal activity follows uneven annual totals: FY21 was $471M, FY22 was $2.2B, FY23 was $1.2B, FY24 was $1.4B, and FY25 was $550M. National Steel and Shipbuilding’s current-year total is partial because FY2026 is year to date. National Steel and Shipbuilding’s FY2026 obligations already exceed several prior full-year totals, reflecting a sharp uptick in award volume and dollar size compared with FY25. National Steel and Shipbuilding’s average award size of $174M implies larger individual awards than in most prior years, given the award count of 16 this year. National Steel and Shipbuilding’s year-over-year change, the award count, and the fiscal-year series give a clear picture of a company with concentrated, high-dollar federal awards in the current fiscal period.",
